---
import Base from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
const crumbs=[{title:"Privacy"}];
---
<Base title="Privacy and Local Tools" description="Learn how Upkeep Atlas uses local homeowner tools, Cloudflare hosting and Google AdSense advertising technology, and what privacy choices apply." breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <section class="page-head"><div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={crumbs}/><span class="eyebrow">A PLAIN-LANGUAGE NOTE</span><h1>Your home details <em class="serif" style="color:var(--pine)">stay yours.</em></h1><p class="lede">Our core tools are designed to work locally in your browser without an account or a street address.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section-small rule-top"><div class="container narrow prose">
    <h2>Planner, calculators and checklists</h2><p>Current planner and calculator selections are calculated in your browser, not sent by our app to a storage service. We do not require a login or uploaded home documents. Checklist checkmarks reset when the page refreshes.</p>
    <h2>Technical hosting data</h2><p>When a website is hosted online, its hosting and network providers may process standard request information such as IP addresses, browser metadata, requested pages and security logs. Upkeep Atlas targets Cloudflare hosting; consult Cloudflare's own privacy documentation for platform practices.</p>
    <h2>Google AdSense and advertising technology</h2>
    <p>Upkeep Atlas includes the Google AdSense advertising script on its configured production website, using publisher ID ca-pub-3399213817491318. The script loads from Google's advertising service. Depending on Google's approval, ad settings and visitor location, Google and its advertising partners may process information such as IP address, browser characteristics, page views and cookie or similar identifiers to serve, limit, measure or personalize advertising. Ads may not be visible until the site is approved and ad formats are turned on.</p>
    <p>We do not intentionally transmit your planner selections, checklist answers or paint-calculator measurements to an advertising API. However, visiting a page that loads third-party code can disclose standard browser and request information to that provider. Learn more from <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's advertising privacy information</a> and manage available personalization preferences through <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">My Ad Center</a>.</p>
    <h2>Regional consent requirements</h2><p>For visitors in the European Economic Area, United Kingdom and Switzerland, Google's advertising rules require a Google-certified consent management platform integrated with the IAB Transparency and Consent Framework when serving eligible ads. The publisher must configure the appropriate privacy and consent messages in AdSense before enabling relevant ad serving; installation of the script alone does not establish compliance. Other regions may have additional disclosure and opt-out requirements.</p>
    <h2>External sources</h2><p>Some pages link to independent websites, including U.S. agencies and ENERGY STAR. Their privacy policies apply when you follow the links.</p>
    <h2>Policy status</h2><p>This page describes the intended product implementation, not a completed legal compliance assessment. Confirm its statements against actual deployment and third-party scripts before launch. Updated November 8, 2026. Appropriate consent configuration and legal review must be completed before relying on this notice for production advertising compliance.</p>
  </div></section>
</Base>
